 pub(crate) fn is_node_with_single_arg_erased<'tcx>(

codex
The MIR dump shows the consume blocks exist but have no incoming edge: the enclosing `!` block still ends `unreachable`. For erased ghost statements, I’m going to explicitly terminate the current connected block with a `Goto` to a fresh successor after lowering preserved subexpressions. If a preserved subexpression really diverged, the returned block is already disconnected, so this does not make real unreachable code reachable.
